d 'TSVY': module to produce point-estimate tables and Wald/CLD tests by level of aggregation and year for complex survey data
d
d    tsvy builds, in one pass, the table that a researcher working
d with repeated cross-sections or panel waves of a complex survey
d usually needs: point estimates (mean, total, proportion or ratio)
d broken down by level of aggregation (national, regional, local,
d ...) and by year, together with a test of whether each level's
d estimate changed from year to year. It loops over every level of
d aggregation named in nivel(), optionally crossed with a second
d variable in cruce(), and for each block reports an omnibus Wald F
d test and a Compact Letter Display of pairwise comparisons
d (Bonferroni by default, escalating to Holm, FDR or LSD only when
d the omnibus test is significant but no pair separates). Results
d accumulate one row per year in a frame ready to reshape and
d export. tsvyexport exports that frame to Excel (.xlsx) or Word
d (.docx), either as is or in a wide year-by-year layout with
d INEI-style table formatting. 
d
d KW: complex survey data
d KW: tabulations
d KW: export
d
d Requires: Stata version 16 and frameappend, (optionally) svylet from SSC (q.v.)
d
d Distribution-Date: 20261124
d
d Author: Andres Talavera Cuya,   Direccion Nacional de Censos y Encuestas -- INEI Peru
d Support: email atalaveracuya@@gmail.com
d
f tsvy.ado
f tsvy.sthlp
f tsvy_es.sthlp
f tsvyexport.ado
f tsvyexport.sthlp
f tsvyexport_es.sthlp
